# .bridgeignore — workspace-local ignore rules for PC File Bridge
#
# Copy this file to your workspace root as ".bridgeignore" and customize it.
# One glob pattern per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Patterns are matched against relative paths using micromatch (glob syntax).
# Both "my-dir" and "my-dir/**" work to exclude a directory and its contents.
#
# These rules are in ADDITION to built-in security defaults (see docs/SECURITY.md).
# They do NOT replace path guards, symlink checks, or the default blocked globs.

# ── Package manager caches (already blocked by default — shown for reference) ──
#
# The following are already in the built-in skip list and do NOT need to be
# added here. Listed for reference only.
#
# .pnpm-store/**
# .yarn/cache/**  .yarn/unplugged/**
# .npm/**
# .bun-install-cache/**
# .nx/cache/**
# .angular/cache/**

# ── Framework output (not built-in — add if your project generates these) ─────

# Framework-specific compiled output
# .output/**
# .svelte-kit/**
# storybook-static/**
# .expo/**
# .expo-shared/**

# ── Build outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Custom build output directory (rename to match your project)
# my-output-dir/**

# Framework-specific compiled output
# .output/**
# .svelte-kit/**
# storybook-static/**

# ── Test and CI artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Test result files
# test-results/**
# playwright-report/**
# junit-results/**

# ── Generated files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Auto-generated code
# generated/**
# __generated__/**
# src/gql/**

# ── Large data or binary directories ─────────────────────────────────────────

# Dataset or model directories (can be large)
# data/**
# models/**
# datasets/**

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Log files
# logs/**
# *.log

# ── Temp directories ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Scratch directories
# tmp/**
# scratch/**
